{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.markovTrace_cyclic_of_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.markovTrace_cyclic_of_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L140-L151","doc":"Any carrier's level-`0` functional is cyclic **and** is the Markov trace, so\n`markovTrace` is forced to be cyclic on the nose.\n\nThis is the point of the rebuild: with the old field types no consequence of this shape\nwas derivable, because the class constrained nothing.  Assuming the conjecture now buys\nsomething. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.GradedMarkovTraceExistence.gradedTrace_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.GradedMarkovTraceExistence.gradedTrace_zero","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L137-L137","doc":"The bottom of the filtration recovers the Markov trace itself — what makes this\nthe descent of `markovTrace` rather than of some unrelated functional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.GradedMarkovTraceExistence.gradedTrace_cyclic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.GradedMarkovTraceExistence.gradedTrace_cyclic","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L134-L134","doc":"Cyclicity — what makes each level's functional a *trace*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.GradedMarkovTraceExistence.gradedTrace_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.GradedMarkovTraceExistence.gradedTrace_add","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L132-L132","doc":"Additivity — part of being the descent of a linear functional. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.GradedMarkovTraceExistence.gradedTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.GradedMarkovTraceExistence.gradedTrace","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L130-L130","doc":"The graded trace **functional** at each filtration level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.GradedMarkovTraceExistence.levelBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.GradedMarkovTraceExistence.levelBound","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L128-L128","doc":"The filtration level bound; concretely `ℓ(K, q)` per `def:confinement-level`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.GradedMarkovTraceExistence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.GradedMarkovTraceExistence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L125-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.GradedMarkovTraceExistence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.GradedMarkovTraceExistence","kind":"class","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L88-L138","doc":"**The graded Markov trace, as a conjecture carrier.**\n\n**Rebuilt 2026-08-30 — this class used to assert nothing.**  It read\n\n```\nclass GradedMarkovTraceExistence (R) [CommRing R] (q : R) (n : ℕ) where\n  levelBound : ℕ\n  gradedTrace : Fin levelBound → R\n```\n\nwith **no `Prop` field at all**: a pair of a natural number and a function into `R`.\nAny such pair inhabits it, and one did — a `default` instance\n`⟨1, fun _ => (0 : R)⟩`, its own comment calling the value a *\"placeholder\"*.  A\n`theorem graded_markov_trace_exists` then closed over `⟨inferInstance⟩` under the\ndocstring *\"Discharge of `conj:gs-graded-markov-trace-existence`\"*.  What that theorem\nestablished is that a pair `(ℕ, Fin 1 → R)` exists.\n\nThis is the `proof-no-empty-prop-carrier` / `proof-claims-unencoded` pattern of\nAGENTS.md §3b-tax, and the old docstring's *\"the substantive existence claim is encoded\nstructurally\"* was the claim §3b-tax exists to catch.\n\nTwo further defects the rebuild fixes:\n\n* **The field had the wrong type.**  The `.md` states `tr_{M,ℓ} : J^ℓ/J^{ℓ+1} → ℝ`, a\n  *functional* on each graded piece.  `Fin levelBound → R` is one **number** per level.\n* **`gradedTrace` was unrelated to `markovTrace`.**  Nothing tied the carrier to the\n  trace it is supposed to be the descent of.\n\nThe fields below carry the conjecture's actual content: each level's functional is\nadditive and cyclic (what makes it a *trace*), and level `0` recovers `markovTrace`\n(what makes it *that* trace's descent).  The filtration itself is not formalised, so\nthese are the properties statable without it — they are deliberately weaker than the\nfull conjecture, and are not claimed to be equivalent to it.\n\n**There is no instance, and that is the honest state**: per §3b-tax an unproved primary\nconjecture is represented by a content-bearing class with no instance.  Supplying one\nis the open work. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:gs-graded-markov-trace-existence","label":"conj:gs-graded-markov-trace-existence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/gs-graded-markov-trace-existence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.markovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovTrace.markovTrace","kind":"opaque","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/MarkovTrace.lean#L67-L79","doc":"**Markov trace signature** on the Type-A Iwahori-Hecke algebra.\n\nSprint 4 deliverable: signature only. The unique functional\nsatisfying the trace + Markov-stabilisation properties is\nconstructed in Sprint 4 follow-up (depends on the reduced-\nexpression basis from Sprint 2 follow-up).\n\nFor now, we declare the signature so downstream consumers can\nreference `markovTrace R q n`; the actual functional content\nis provided by §3b-cond instances of `MarkovTraceClass` below. ","signatureChunk":0}]}